update public.moo_versions set body_md = body_md || E'Beneficiary lists, household damage records and case files are personal or sensitive personal information under RA 10173. They are held by the office that serves the person, with access limited to staff who need them. The monitoring matrix, MODE and public reports carry aggregates by barangay and by PPA only. Small counts that could identify a person are referred to the City Data Protection Officer before publication.\n\n## 13.5 Outcome Evaluation and Learning\n\nFor a large event the CDRRMC commissions an outcome evaluation of the whole program or selected sectors, to check whether the target outcomes were achieved and whether the PPAs contributed to them. Projects are selected using criteria such as number of beneficiaries, contribution to local income, jobs generated and basic services provided. The evaluation is participatory and supervised by the monitoring unit even when a third party conducts it (NEDA, 2020). Its findings, together with the AAR from Chapter 4 (ER-F06), go to the Chapter 7 corrective-action register and revise the pre-disaster recovery framework.\n\n## 13.6 MODE Platform Support\n\nMODE does not yet hold a recovery module. Forms ER-F05 and ER-F06 from Chapter 4 are loaded in the SOP registry, and the Data Dictionary lists recovery entities (recovery assessments, plans, actions, service referrals and frameworks) for functional area 10 (MR-11). Once this chapter is seeded, its SOPs are carried as Library drafts and as workflows or protocols, and forms REC-F01 to REC-F09 are configured as step forms. The monitoring matrix can be kept in a controlled workbook until a MODE screen is built. Seeded content stays a draft until the owning office validates it and the CDRRMO Head approves it.\n\n# 14. Standard Operating Procedures\n\nThe following procedures set the minimum control sequence for recovery. Before adoption, the CDRRMO shall reconcile them with the current OCD PDNA Guidance Notes, the City''s approval routes and the IAT v1.7 Action Plan (Annex 5-A). Each procedure shall be loaded in MODE as a workflow (a multi-office management cycle) or a protocol (a point-of-action checklist) and tested through a tabletop exercise or, for SOP 5-02, a PDNA simulation.\n\nFigure 5.6 places the eight procedures in the recovery phases. Each procedure has a control block (type, the proposed MODE template, the legal decision authority kept apart from the operational owner, trigger, forms, indicators and policy basis) and a step table. Every step states its actor, action, decision or criteria, inputs, outputs and records, timing, control and escalation.\n\n**Figure 5.6**\n\n*Chapter 5 Procedures by Recovery Phase*\n\n![Figure 6: 14. Standard Operating Procedures](/library/chp5v10/fig-06.webp)\n\n*Note.* Form codes are those of section 18. All MODE templates named in the control blocks are proposals; none is yet loaded in MODE.\n\n## SOP 5-01 \\| Pre-disaster recovery framework: preparation, adoption and annual update\n\n**Process owner:** CDRRMO Research and Planning, with CPDO as technical lead. **Purpose:** Have roles, PDNA activation, temporary shelter, debris management, scalable PPAs and recovery fund sources agreed before an event.\n\n**Table 5.17**\n\n*SOP 5-01 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                                                                |\n|---------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Workflow: WF-REC-FRAMEWORK (6 steps, proposed)                                                                                           |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | CDRRMC adopts the framework; Sangguniang Panlungsod for any appropriation or ordinance it requires                                       |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | CDRRMO Head; CDRRMO Research and Planning with CPDO                                                                                      |\n| **Trigger**                     | Annual planning cycle (aligned with LDRRMP and LDRRMFIP preparation); after an event that triggered a PDNA; after a material plan change |\n| **Forms**                       | REC-F01; Annex 5-C outline; Annex 5-E data list                                                                                          |\n| **IAT v1.7 indicators**         | A9.5 (score 1, Medium); A3.4 (score 2, Medium)                                                                                           |\n| **Functional MR links**         | A9.5: MR-11, MR-18; A3.4: MR-10                                                                                                          |\n| **Policy basis**                | RA 10121; NEDA (2020) Part 2 §I; UNDRR Scorecard Essential 10                                                                            |\n| **Cross-references**            | Chapter 3 (CDRA, SOP 3-06 contingency plans, PSCP); Chapter 6 (LDRRMFIP)                                                                 |\n\n**Table 5.18**\n\n*SOP 5-01 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 20%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Update baseline</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Research and Planning</th>\n<th><p>Refresh the recovery baseline by barangay from CDRA, CBMS, PSA and office data (Annex 5-E).</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Is each dataset dated and sourced? Mark gaps as "not reported", not zero.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Chapter 3 risk data; office datasets</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Updated baseline; data-gap list</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Q1 each year</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Source and date on every dataset</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head for missing office data</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Set scenarios</th>\n<th>CDRRMO with CPDO</th>\n<th><p>Take the most-probable and most-severe scenario per priority hazard from the CDRA and contingency plans; estimate recovery needs.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Same scenarios as Chapter 3? If not, record why.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> CDRA; CP scenarios</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Recovery scenario sheet</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Q1</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Assumptions stated</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Technical agency for disputed parameters</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Agree organisation</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head</th>\n<th><p>Confirm sub-committee leads, members and focal persons (Table 5.10); confirm PDNA team designations.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Has each lead office accepted its role in writing?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Sub-committee proposal</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Signed focal-person list; draft office order</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Q2</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Positions named, not only persons</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC Chair if an office declines</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. List scalable PPAs</th>\n<th>Each lead office</th>\n<th><p>Submit regular PPAs that can be scaled up or reprogrammed, with outputs, unit costs and approval needed.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Is the realignment authority identified?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Office work plans and AIP</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Scalable PPA list</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Q2</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> One list per office, dated</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Map financing</th>\n<th>City Budget Office with CDRRMO</th>\n<th><p>Record recovery fund options (Table 5.11), insurance status of City assets and enrolment status of farmers.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Any asset uninsured or fund rule unclear? Record and refer.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> LDRRMFIP; GSIS records</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Financing map</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Q2, before budget preparation</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Chapter 6 rules applied</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> City Treasurer; Chapter 6 owner</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Adopt and attach</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head; CDRRMC</th>\n<th><p>Consolidate into the framework (Annex 5-C); present to the CDRRMC; attach as recovery annex of each contingency plan.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Adopted? If not, record the changes asked for.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Steps 1–5 outputs</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> CDRRMC resolution; framework; REC-F01 entry</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Q2–Q3</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Version and adoption date recorded; Library draft until approved</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC Chair</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Recovery baseline; scenario sheet; focal-person list; scalable PPA lists; financing map; adopted framework and CDRRMC resolution; REC-F01 register.\n\n## SOP 5-02 \\| Damage and needs assessment: RDANA to PDNA decision and PDNA conduct\n\n**Process owner:** CDRRMO Head as PDNA lead; designated PDNA team. **Purpose:** Decide on, carry out and approve a PDNA that gives the program a reliable account of damage, losses and recovery needs.\n\n**Table 5.19**\n\n*SOP 5-02 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                                        |\n|---------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Protocol: PR-PDNA (7 steps, proposed)                                                                            |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | CDRRMC decides whether to conduct the PDNA and approves it; RDRRMC VIII reviews it when NDRRMF funding is sought |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | CDRRMO Head; PDNA team coordinator                                                                               |\n| **Trigger**                     | RDANA shows damage in two or more barangays; State of Calamity declared; national assistance needed              |\n| **Forms**                       | REC-F03; RDANA forms (Chapter 4); OCD PDNA templates                                                             |\n| **IAT v1.7 indicators**         | A9.1 (score 1, Medium); A8.7 (score 2, Medium)                                                                   |\n| **Functional MR links**         | A9.1: MR-11; A8.7: MR-05                                                                                         |\n| **Policy basis**                | RA 10121; NEDA (2020) Part 2 §II.A; OCD PDNA Guidance Notes                                                      |\n| **Cross-references**            | SOP 4-08 (SitRep), SOP 4-09; SOP 5-04                                                                            |\n\n**Table 5.20**\n\n*SOP 5-02 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 20%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Review RDANA</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head with PDNA coordinator</th>\n<th><p>Review RDANA results, SitReps and the extent of damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Two or more barangays affected and a trigger met? Prepare a recommendation either way.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> RDANA; SitReps; SoC declaration if any</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> PDNA recommendation note</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> As soon as response stabilises</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Source of each figure stated</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Mayor if the CDRRMC cannot meet promptly</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Decide</th>\n<th>CDRRMC</th>\n<th><p>Decide whether to conduct a City PDNA, its scope and whether to request OCD VIII support or a RaDE first.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> PDNA, RaDE first, or no PDNA (with reasons)?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Recommendation note</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> CDRRMC resolution or minutes; REC-F03 part 1</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Next CDRRMC meeting or special meeting</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Decision and reasons recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> RDRRMC VIII when Ormoc and another LGU are affected</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Mobilise team</th>\n<th>PDNA coordinator</th>\n<th><p>Activate the designated team by sector; brief on method, templates, safety and privacy.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> All priority sectors covered? Fill gaps from sub-committee offices.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Office order; templates</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Team list; briefing record</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within days of the decision</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Positions named; data rules briefed</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head; OCD VIII for technical support</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Collect and validate</th>\n<th>Sector teams</th>\n<th><p>Collect damage and loss data by sector and barangay; validate in the field; record human recovery needs.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Confirmed or for validation? Source recorded.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Baseline; field data; agency data</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Sector damage and loss sheets</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> As set in the OCD Guidance Notes</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Aggregates only in shared sheets</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> PDNA coordinator for access or safety problems</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Analyse</th>\n<th>PDNA coordinator with CPDO</th>\n<th><p>Compute damage, losses and needs; estimate economic impact; summarise the situation of vulnerable groups.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Are unit costs and assumptions stated?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Sector sheets</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Draft PDNA report</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> After field work</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Calculations reproducible</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Sub-committee lead for disputed sector figures</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Approve</th>\n<th>CDRRMC</th>\n<th><p>Review and approve the PDNA report.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Approved, or returned with corrections?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Draft PDNA</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Approved PDNA; REC-F03 part 2</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Next meeting</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Version control; superseded drafts kept</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC Chair</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>7. Transmit</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head</th>\n<th><p>Send the PDNA to the program team (SOP 5-04) and, where national funding is sought, to RDRRMC VIII for review.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> National funding needed?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Approved PDNA</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Transmittal records</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> On approval</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Receipt acknowledged</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> OCD VIII</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** PDNA recommendation; CDRRMC decision; team list and briefing; sector sheets; PDNA report with assumptions; approval and transmittal records (REC-F03).\n\n## SOP 5-03 \\| Response-to-recovery transition and early recovery coordination\n\n**Process owner:** CDRRMO Head, with the EOC Manager handing over and the recovery lead offices receiving. **Purpose:** Make sure every open item on the Chapter 4 transition register has a named recovery owner and that early recovery starts without a gap.\n\n**Table 5.21**\n\n*SOP 5-03 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                                 |\n|---------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Protocol: PR-RECOVERY-TRANSITION (6 steps, proposed)                                                      |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | Deactivation authority under the EOC EO (Chapter 4); CDRRMC for the activation of recovery sub-committees |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | CDRRMO Head                                                                                               |\n| **Trigger**                     | EOC deactivation or scale-down under SOP 4-09; ER-F05 issued                                              |\n| **Forms**                       | ER-F05 (Chapter 4); REC-F02                                                                               |\n| **IAT v1.7 indicators**         | A9.4 (score 2, Low); A10.6 (score 2, Medium)                                                              |\n| **Functional MR links**         | A9.4: MR-11; A10.6: MR-07, MR-11                                                                          |\n| **Policy basis**                | NEDA (2020) Part 2; JMC No. 2 s. 2021; Chapter 4 SOP 4-09                                                 |\n| **Cross-references**            | SOP 4-09; SOP 5-02, 5-06, 5-07                                                                            |\n\n**Table 5.22**\n\n*SOP 5-03 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 20%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Receive register</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head</th>\n<th><p>Receive the ER-F05 transition register and the ER-F06 AAR record from the EOC Manager.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Is every item described with location, scale and current owner?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> ER-F05; ER-F06</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> REC-F02 intake entries</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> At deactivation</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Each ER-F05 line gets a REC-F02 line</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> EOC Manager for incomplete items</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Assign owners</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head with sub-committee leads</th>\n<th><p>Assign each open item to the office that holds the mandate; record due date.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Which office holds the mandate? Never assign to CDRRMO by default.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> REC-F02</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Owner and due date per item</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within the first week after deactivation</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Owner accepts in writing</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Mayor for disputed ownership</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Activate sub-committees</th>\n<th>CDRRMC Chair</th>\n<th><p>Activate the sub-committees the event needs, using the framework.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Which sectors are affected?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Framework; PDNA decision</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Activation notice</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> With the PDNA decision</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Only needed sub-committees activated</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Close evacuation centres safely</th>\n<th>CSWDO with barangays</th>\n<th><p>Plan return or alternative shelter for remaining displaced families before closing centres; restore schools.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Do families have a safe place to go?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Aggregate displacement data</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Closure plan; durable-solution referrals</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before each closure</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> No closure without a plan for remaining families</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head; Mayor</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Start early recovery</th>\n<th>Lead offices</th>\n<th><p>Start scalable PPAs (cash-for-work, shelter repair aid, input distribution, debris clearing) under existing authorities.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Within existing authority and budget? If not, refer to Chapter 6.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Scalable PPA list</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Early recovery entries in REC-F06</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> As soon as safe</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Fund source recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Resource mobilisation sub-committee</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Report</th>\n<th>CDRRMO</th>\n<th><p>Report the status of all transferred items to the CDRRMC until each is closed or moved into the program.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Any item overdue?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> REC-F02; REC-F06</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Transition status report</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Every CDRRMC meeting</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Closed items show evidence</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC Chair</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** ER-F05 and ER-F06 as received; REC-F02 intake and assignment entries; activation notice; evacuation centre closure plans; transition status reports.\n\n## SOP 5-04 \\| Rehabilitation and recovery program: formulation, approval and updating\n\n**Process owner:** CPDO as technical lead with the CDRRMO; Rehabilitation and Recovery Committee. **Purpose:** Produce a program with build-back-better and resettlement provisions, approved through the proper route and kept up to date.\n\n**Table 5.23**\n\n*SOP 5-04 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                                      |\n|---------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Workflow: WF-REC-PROGRAM (7 steps, proposed)                                                                   |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | CDRRMC prepares and endorses; Sangguniang Panlungsod approves; NDRRMC through RDRRMC VIII for national funding |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | CPDO technical lead; CDRRMO secretariat                                                                        |\n| **Trigger**                     | State of Calamity declared; national assistance needed; or CDRRMC decision after a PDNA                        |\n| **Forms**                       | REC-F04; Annex 5-C; Table 5.13                                                                                 |\n| **IAT v1.7 indicators**         | A9.2 (score 2, Medium, Mandatory)                                                                              |\n| **Functional MR links**         | A9.2: MR-11                                                                                                    |\n| **Policy basis**                | RA 10121; RA 7160; NEDA (2020) Part 2 §II                                                                      |\n| **Cross-references**            | SOP 5-02, 5-05; Chapter 6 (budget and procurement)                                                             |\n\n**Table 5.24**\n\n*SOP 5-04 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 20%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Organise</th>\n<th>CDRRMC Chair</th>\n<th><p>Convene the Rehabilitation and Recovery Committee and its activated sub-committees; confirm the planning schedule.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Interim priority PPAs needed before the full program?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Framework; PDNA decision</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Planning schedule</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> With the PDNA decision</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Schedule shared with all offices</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Mayor</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Frame</th>\n<th>CPDO with CDRRMO</th>\n<th><p>Draft the recovery framework, objectives and strategies from the PDNA and the City''s development plans.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Outcomes consistent with CDP and LDRRMP?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> PDNA; CDP; LDRRMP</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Draft framework and objectives</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> After PDNA approval</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Each objective traced to a PDNA finding</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CPDO head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Identify PPAs</th>\n<th>Sub-committees</th>\n<th><p>Identify and cost PPAs by sector, location and phase; screen each with SOP 5-05.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Passed BBB screening?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> PDNA needs; scalable PPA list</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Draft PPA list (REC-F04); REC-F07 screens</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within the planning schedule</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Unit costs and sources stated</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Sub-committee lead</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Budget review</th>\n<th>Resource mobilisation sub-committee</th>\n<th><p>Match PPAs to fund sources; identify the gap and options (supplemental budget, NDRRMF, partners).</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Gap covered? If not, which route?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> REC-F04; financing map</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Investment requirement by source and by sector</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Alongside step 3</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Chapter 6 rules applied</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> City Budget Officer; Mayor</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Consult</th>\n<th>CDRRMO with barangays</th>\n<th><p>Consult affected barangays and sector representatives on the draft, including women, PWD and older persons.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Changes needed from consultation?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Draft program</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Consultation record</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before endorsement</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Attendance disaggregated</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Endorse and approve</th>\n<th>CDRRMC; Sangguniang Panlungsod</th>\n<th><p>CDRRMC endorses; the Sanggunian approves the program and appropriations; submit through RDRRMC VIII if national funds are sought.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Approved? Interim PPAs approved first if needed.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Final draft</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Resolution and ordinance; transmittal</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> As soon as ready</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Approved version locked; changes by superseding version</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> City Legal Office on route questions</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>7. Update</th>\n<th>CPDO with monitoring unit</th>\n<th><p>Revise PPAs and the investment program based on accomplishment reports.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Material change needing re-approval?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> SOP 5-07 reports</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Updated program version</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> At least annually</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Version history kept</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Planning schedule; framework and objectives; REC-F04 PPA list; REC-F07 screens; investment tables; consultation record; endorsement and approval instruments; version history.\n\n## SOP 5-05 \\| Build-back-better screening of recovery projects\n\n**Process owner:** Proponent office, with the Building Official, CPDO/Zoning Administrator and ENRO as reviewers. **Purpose:** Make sure each recovery project reduces risk compared with the pre-disaster situation before it is funded.\n\n**Table 5.25**\n\n*SOP 5-05 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                                                         |\n|---------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Protocol: PR-BBB-SCREEN (6 steps, proposed)                                                                                       |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | No new authority: permits, siting and design decisions stay with the Building Official, Zoning Administrator and approving bodies |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | Proponent office; Infrastructure or Shelter sub-committee lead                                                                    |\n| **Trigger**                     | Any recovery PPA that builds, repairs, relocates or restores a structure, lifeline, settlement or ecosystem                       |\n| **Forms**                       | REC-F07                                                                                                                           |\n| **IAT v1.7 indicators**         | A9.2 (score 2, Medium); C1.4 (score 2, Medium); C2.1 (score 1, High); C2.2 (score 2, Medium)                                      |\n| **Functional MR links**         | A9.2: MR-11; Part C rows report to the Interface Index, not the IMI                                                               |\n| **Policy basis**                | PD 1096; RA 12076; CLUP and Zoning Ordinance; NEDA (2020); Sendai Priority 4                                                      |\n| **Cross-references**            | Section 9; Chapter 3 hazard maps; Chapter 8 (Part C interfaces)                                                                   |\n\n**Table 5.26**\n\n*SOP 5-05 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 20%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Describe</th>\n<th>Proponent office</th>\n<th><p>Describe the project, location, pre-disaster condition and cause of damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Is the cause of damage known?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> PDNA; site data</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> REC-F07 part 1</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before costing is final</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Photos and location recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Sub-committee lead</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Check hazard and siting</th>\n<th>CPDO / Zoning Administrator</th>\n<th><p>Overlay hazard maps; check CLUP and Zoning Ordinance.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Rebuild in place, rebuild with measures, or relocate?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Hazard maps; CLUP; ZO</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Siting finding</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within the planning schedule</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Map version cited</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CPDO head; refer gaps in the ZO to the Sanggunian</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Check design</th>\n<th>Building Official / City Engineer</th>\n<th><p>Check design against the structural code in force, flood levels and the hazard.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Meets the standard? If not, what change?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Design; assessment</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Design finding</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before approval</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Signed by the reviewer</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> City Engineer</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Check people and environment</th>\n<th>CSWDO; ENRO</th>\n<th><p>Check accessibility, inclusion, displacement effects and environmental impact.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Any group made worse off? Any environmental harm?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Design; site data</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Inclusion and environment findings</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before approval</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Mitigation recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Sub-committee lead</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Decide</th>\n<th>Sub-committee lead</th>\n<th><p>Record pass, pass with conditions, or redesign.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> All findings resolved?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Findings</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> REC-F07 decision</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before funding</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Conditions carried into the PPA</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Rehabilitation and Recovery Committee</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Verify</th>\n<th>Monitoring unit</th>\n<th><p>At completion, check that the conditions were built.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Conditions met?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> REC-F07; completion report</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Verification entry in REC-F06</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> At completion</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Site visit for key projects</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** REC-F07 screen with siting, design, inclusion and environment findings; decision and conditions; completion verification.\n\n## SOP 5-06 \\| Psychosocial, social protection and livelihood referral pathway\n\n**Process owner:** CSWDO as pathway coordinator, with CHO, PESO, BPLO, City Agriculture and the housing office. **Purpose:** Connect affected people to the recovery services they need through one screening and referral process, with consent and privacy.\n\n**Table 5.27**\n\n*SOP 5-06 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                  |\n|---------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Protocol: PR-RECOVERY-REFERRAL (6 steps, proposed)                         |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | Each receiving office decides eligibility under its own rules              |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | CSWDO (coordinator); receiving offices                                     |\n| **Trigger**                     | Need identified at a camp desk, barangay, health facility or feedback desk |\n| **Forms**                       | REC-F05 (restricted)                                                       |\n| **IAT v1.7 indicators**         | A9.4 (score 2, Low)                                                        |\n| **Functional MR links**         | A9.4: MR-11                                                                |\n| **Policy basis**                | RA 11036; JMC No. 2 s. 2021; RA 10173; RA 9710; RA 7277 as amended         |\n| **Cross-references**            | Section 10.1; SOP 5-08; Chapter 4 SOP 4-06                                 |\n\n**Table 5.28**\n\n*SOP 5-06 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 20%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Identify</th>\n<th>Entry-point staff</th>\n<th><p>Identify a recovery need and explain the referral and how data will be used.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Does the person consent?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Interview</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Consent noted on REC-F05</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> At contact</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> No referral without consent, except where the law allows (e.g., child protection)</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CSWDO for protection concerns</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Screen</th>\n<th>Entry-point staff</th>\n<th><p>Record need categories and urgency using the minimum fields of REC-F05.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Urgent (safety, health)? Refer at once.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Interview</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> REC-F05 screening</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> At contact</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Minimum data only</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CHO or CSWDO duty officer for urgent cases</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Refer</th>\n<th>Entry-point staff</th>\n<th><p>Send the referral to the receiving office through the agreed channel.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Which office holds the service?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> REC-F05</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Referral sent; receipt</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Same day where possible</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Receipt acknowledged</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Pathway coordinator</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Serve</th>\n<th>Receiving office</th>\n<th><p>Assess eligibility and provide or schedule the service.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Eligible? If not, refer onward or explain.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Referral</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Service record (office''s own restricted record)</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> As set by the office</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Reason recorded for refusals</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Office head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Feed back</th>\n<th>Receiving office</th>\n<th><p>Update the referral status and inform the person.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Closed, ongoing or referred onward?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Service record</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Status update</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> On each change</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Person informed</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Pathway coordinator</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Report aggregates</th>\n<th>CSWDO</th>\n<th><p>Report referrals by type, status, barangay, sex, age group and disability to the monitoring unit.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Small counts that could identify a person? Ask the DPO.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Status updates</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Aggregate referral report</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Monthly during the program</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> No names in the report</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> DPO; CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** REC-F05 (restricted, held by the referring and receiving offices); service records of each office; aggregate referral reports. MOAs or a joint office order among CSWDO, CHO and PESO set the channels.\n\n> VALIDATION NOTE. The pathway needs a written agreement (MOA or joint office order) among CSWDO, CHO, PESO, BPLO, City Agriculture and the housing office, which is the recommended action for A9.4. The City Data Protection Officer shall review REC-F05, the consent wording and the retention period before use.\n\n## SOP 5-07 \\| Recovery monitoring, tracking to completion and closeout\n\n**Process owner:** Recovery monitoring unit (CDRRMO Research and Planning with CPDO monitoring staff). **Purpose:** Track every recovery PPA, whatever its fund source, from approval to completion and evaluate the outcome.\n\n**Table 5.29**\n\n*SOP 5-07 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                             |\n|---------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Workflow: WF-REC-MONITOR (7 steps, proposed)                                                          |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | CDRRMC receives reports and decides corrective actions; outcome evaluation commissioned by the CDRRMC |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | Recovery monitoring unit                                                                              |\n| **Trigger**                     | Program approved (or first early recovery PPA started)                                                |\n| **Forms**                       | REC-F06; REC-F09; Annex 5-D                                                                           |\n| **IAT v1.7 indicators**         | A9.3 (score 1, Low); A10.6 (score 2, Medium)                                                          |\n| **Functional MR links**         | A9.3: MR-11; A10.6: MR-07, MR-11                                                                      |\n| **Policy basis**                | NEDA (2020) Part 5; Sendai Framework Targets C and D                                                  |\n| **Cross-references**            | Chapter 6 (financial reports); Chapter 7 (AAR, corrective action, knowledge management)               |\n\n**Table 5.30**\n\n*SOP 5-07 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 20%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Set up matrix</th>\n<th>Monitoring unit</th>\n<th><p>Load all approved PPAs into REC-F06 with targets, budget, fund source, office and schedule.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Every PPA entered, including partner-funded ones?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Approved program; REC-F04</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> REC-F06 baseline</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within a month of approval</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> One matrix for all sources</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Name focal persons</th>\n<th>Implementing offices</th>\n<th><p>Name a monitoring focal person for each office.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Every office covered?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Office list</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Focal-person list</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> With step 1</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Positions named</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC Chair</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Report progress</th>\n<th>Office focal persons</th>\n<th><p>Report physical and financial accomplishment, issues and next steps.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Behind schedule or over cost?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Office records</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Progress report</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Monthly in year 1, then quarterly (proposed)</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Figures reconcile with Accounting</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Monitoring unit</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Solve problems</th>\n<th>Monitoring unit</th>\n<th><p>Hold the inter-office problem-solving meeting; record decisions and owners.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Can the issue be solved at office level?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Progress reports</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Issue log and decisions</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Monthly</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Each issue has an owner and date</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC for policy or funding issues</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Validate in the field</th>\n<th>Monitoring unit with focal persons</th>\n<th><p>Visit key and problem projects; verify outputs and BBB conditions.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Do reported outputs exist on the ground?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> REC-F06; REC-F07</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Field validation notes</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Quarterly, and for each key completion</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Photos and dates recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Report to CDRRMC</th>\n<th>Monitoring unit</th>\n<th><p>Consolidate a status report and snapshot for the CDRRMC and the public.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Corrective decisions needed?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Steps 3–5</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Status report; public snapshot</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Each CDRRMC meeting; at least annually</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Same figures in internal and public reports</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC Chair</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>7. Close and evaluate</th>\n<th>Monitoring unit</th>\n<th><p>Close each PPA with evidence; for large events, run the outcome evaluation and send lessons to Chapter 7.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> All PPAs closed or carried into regular programs?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Completion evidence</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> REC-F09 closeout; evaluation report; lessons</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> At program end</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Closure only with evidence</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** REC-F06 matrix and its versions; focal-person list; progress reports; issue log; field validation notes; CDRRMC status reports and public snapshots; REC-F09 closeout and evaluation.\n\n## SOP 5-08 \\| Recovery communication, feedback and grievance handling\n\n**Process owner:** Designated recovery spokesperson and communication focal person; CDRRMO feedback desk. **Purpose:** Keep affected people informed and give them a channel to raise problems and get an answer.\n\n**Table 5.31**\n\n*SOP 5-08 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                                         |\n|---------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Protocol: PR-REC-FEEDBACK (6 steps, proposed)                                                                     |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | Mayor or designated spokesperson approves public statements; each office decides on grievances within its mandate |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | Communication focal person; CDRRMO feedback desk                                                                  |\n| **Trigger**                     | Program start; each release date; each feedback or grievance received                                             |\n| **Forms**                       | REC-F08                                                                                                           |\n| **IAT v1.7 indicators**         | A9.4 (score 2, Low); A9.2 (score 2, Medium)                                                                       |\n| **Functional MR links**         | A9.4, A9.2: MR-11                                                                                                 |\n| **Policy basis**                | NEDA (2020) Part 4 §III; RA 10173; Chapter 1 full-disclosure provisions                                           |\n| **Cross-references**            | Section 12; SOP 5-06, 5-07                                                                                        |\n\n**Table 5.32**\n\n*SOP 5-08 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 20%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Adopt strategy</th>\n<th>CDRRMC</th>\n<th><p>Adopt the communication strategy (Table 5.16); designate the spokesperson and focal person.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Strategy covers all five components?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Program draft</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Adopted strategy</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> At program start</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Names of positions recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Mayor</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Publish updates</th>\n<th>Comms focal person</th>\n<th><p>Publish progress updates on the agreed schedule, using matrix figures.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Figures match REC-F06?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Status report</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Public update</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Per schedule</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Approved before release</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Spokesperson</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Receive feedback</th>\n<th>Feedback desk; barangays</th>\n<th><p>Receive feedback and grievances through all channels, including in person.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Grievance, question or suggestion? Protection concern?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Message or visit</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> REC-F08 entry</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> On receipt</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Acknowledged to the person</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CSWDO at once for protection concerns</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Route</th>\n<th>Feedback desk</th>\n<th><p>Send each grievance to the office that holds the mandate.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Which office?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> REC-F08</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Routing record</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within the period set by the CDRRMC</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Receipt by the office</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Resolve and reply</th>\n<th>Receiving office</th>\n<th><p>Investigate, act and reply to the person.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Resolved, or explained why not?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Grievance</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Reply; status update</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within the period set by the CDRRMC</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Reply recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Office head; CDRRMC for repeated issues</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Learn</th>\n<th>Comms focal person</th>\n<th><p>Summarise feedback trends for the CDRRMC and the monitoring unit.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Patterns needing program change?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> REC-F08</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Feedback summary</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> With each status report</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Aggregates only</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Adopted strategy; public updates and corrections; REC-F08 log (personal details restricted); routing and reply records; feedback summaries.\n\n# 15. Responsibility Assignment (RACI)\n\nThe following RACI is a proposed operational assignment for validation. "A" is the single process-accountable owner for the operational task; "R" performs the work; "C" is consulted; "I" is informed. It does not transfer statutory powers. Where a legal decision belongs to a named body, that body is stated separately in the SOP control block and in Annex 5-B.\n\n**Table 5.33**\n\n*Proposed Recovery RACI*\n\n| **Activity**                       | **Mayor / SP**   | **CDRRMC**  | **CDRRMO** | **CPDO**           | **Sector offices** | **Budget / BAC** | **Barangays** |\n|------------------------------------|------------------|-------------|------------|--------------------|--------------------|------------------|---------------|\n| Pre-disaster recovery framework    | I                | A (adopt)   | R          | R                  | C                  | C                | C             |\n| Recovery baseline and scenarios    | I                | I           | A/R        | R                  | C                  | I                | C             |\n| PDNA decision and approval         | I                | A           | R          | C                  | C                  | I                | I             |\n| PDNA conduct                       | I                | I           | A/R        | R                  | R                  | I                | C             |\n| Response-to-recovery transition    | I                | I           | A          | C                  | R                  | I                | R             |\n| Program formulation                | I                | A (endorse) | R          | R (technical lead) | R                  | R                | C             |\n| Program approval and appropriation | A (SP)           | R           | C          | C                  | I                  | C                | I             |\n| BBB screening                      | I                | I           | C          | R                  | A/R (proponent)    | I                | C             |\n| Service delivery and referrals     | I                | I           | C          | I                  | A/R                | I                | R             |\n| Financing and procurement          | A (approvals)    | C           | C          | C                  | R                  | R                | I             |\n| Monitoring to completion           | I                | I           | A/R        | R                  | R                  | R                | C             |\n| Communication and grievances       | A (spokesperson) | C           | R          | C                  | R                  | I                | R             |\n| Outcome evaluation and lessons     | I                | A           | R          | R                  | R                  | C                | C             |\n\n*Note.* SP = Sangguniang Panlungsod. "Sector offices" are the lead offices of the sub-committees in Table 5.10.\n\n# 16. Performance Monitoring, Quality Assurance and Corrective Action\n\nPerformance is monitored through a small set of measures with evidence. Numerical targets are set by the CDRRMC in the framework or the program; this draft does not impose them.\n\n**Table 5.34**\n\n*Recovery Performance Areas, Measures and Review Owners*\n\n| **Performance area** | **Suggested measure / evidence**                                                                                               | **Review owner**                  |\n|----------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------|\n| **Readiness**        | Framework adopted and reviewed in the year; recovery annex present in each contingency plan; PDNA team designated and trained. | CDRRMO Head; CDRRMC               |\n| **Transition**       | Share of ER-F05 items with a named recovery owner within the period set by the CDRRMC; items closed with evidence.             | CDRRMO Head                       |\n| **Assessment**       | PDNA decision recorded; PDNA approved; assumptions documented.                                                                 | CDRRMC                            |\n| **Programming**      | Program approved; PPAs traced to PDNA needs; BBB screens complete for all physical PPAs.                                       | CPDO; CDRRMC                      |\n| **Delivery**         | Physical and financial accomplishment against targets by sector and barangay; issues resolved.                                 | Monitoring unit                   |\n| **Inclusion**        | Beneficiaries and consultation participants disaggregated by sex, age and disability; grievances answered.                     | CSWDO; communication focal person |\n| **Outcome**          | Evaluation findings on restored conditions and reduced risk; lessons recorded in Chapter 7.                                    | CDRRMC                            |\n\nCorrective actions follow Chapter 7: each records the finding, evidence, cause, action, owner, supporting offices, due date, resource implication, verification and closure decision. Repeated non-closure is escalated through the CDRRMO Head to the CDRRMC.\n\n# 17. Implementation, Validation and Institutionalisation Priorities\n\nThe priorities below come from the IAT v1.7 Action Plan and the gaps described in section 1. Annex 5-A gives the owners, targets and status exactly as recorded in the workbook.\n\n**Table 5.35**\n\n*Implementation, Validation and Institutionalisation Priorities*\n\n| **Reference**                 | **Required action**                                                                                                                       | **Proposed accountable lead**                                     | **Evidence of completion / validation**                                              |\n|-------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| P1 – A9.5 (Medium)            | Prepare and adopt the pre-disaster recovery framework using the Ready to Rebuild workbook; attach it to the contingency plans (SOP 5-01). | CDRRMO Research and Planning; CPDO                                | CDRRMC resolution; framework; recovery annexes; tabletop exercise.                   |\n| P1 – A8.7, A9.1 (Medium)      | Designate RDANA, MDM and PDNA teams by EO or office order; train them with OCD VIII; keep templates ready (SOP 5-02).                     | CDRRMO; CHO; PNP (A8.7); CDRRMO Research and Planning (A9.1)      | Issuance; certificates; templates in the Library; PDNA simulation.                   |\n| P1 – A9.2 (Medium, Mandatory) | Attach existing rehabilitation plans and implementation reports for validation; adopt SOP 5-04 for the next event.                        | CDRRMO                                                            | Plans and reports in the Vault; validated score.                                     |\n| P2 – A9.3 (Low)               | Set up the recovery monitoring matrix (REC-F06) in the event database (SOP 5-07).                                                         | CDRRMO Research and Planning                                      | Matrix in use for the latest event; status report to the CDRRMC.                     |\n| P2 – A9.4 (Low)               | Sign the referral agreement among CSWDO, CHO and PESO (and BPLO, City Agriculture, housing office) (SOP 5-06).                            | CSWDO; CHO; PESO                                                  | MOA or joint office order; REC-F05 reviewed by the DPO; referral reports.            |\n| P2 – Recovery committee       | Create the Rehabilitation and Recovery Committee and its sub-committees, or assign the function to the CDRRMP TWG (EO 2022-00020).        | CDRRMC; City Legal Office                                         | Issuance; focal-person list.                                                         |\n| P2 – C1.4, C2.1–C2.3 (Part C) | Agree with the Building Official, Zoning Administrator and utilities how BBB screening and restoration priorities work (SOP 5-05).        | City Engineer; CPDO; utilities (lead offices); CDRRMO coordinates | Screening form adopted; restoration-priority arrangements; Interface Index evidence. |\n\n*Note.* Part C rows are reported in the separate Interface Index and are never added to the Institutional Maturity Index.\n\n# 18. Forms, Registers and Annexes\n\nThe following forms operationalise the chapter. They shall be configured as controlled forms and linked to the protocol and workflow steps in the Library and MODE. Forms that hold personal information are restricted records of the office that owns them.\n\n**Table 5.36**\n\n*Chapter 5 Forms, Registers and Annexes*\n\n| **Code**  | **Title**                                           | **Purpose / key fields**                                                                                | **Primary user / custodian**              |\n|-----------|-----------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|\n| REC-F01   | Pre-disaster recovery framework register            | Version, adoption date, CDRRMC resolution, review date, attached contingency plans, open gaps.          | CDRRMO Research and Planning              |\n| REC-F02   | Recovery transition intake and assignment record    | ER-F05 line reference, item, location, scale, receiving office, due date, status, closure evidence.     | CDRRMO Head                               |\n| REC-F03   | PDNA decision, team and approval record             | Trigger, decision and reasons, scope, team by sector, OCD VIII support, approval, transmittal.          | PDNA coordinator                          |\n| REC-F04   | Rehabilitation and recovery PPA list                | PPA, sector, location, phase, cost, annual breakdown, fund source, implementing office, PDNA reference. | CPDO; resource mobilisation sub-committee |\n| REC-F05   | Recovery screening and referral record (restricted) | Consent, need categories, urgency, referring and receiving office, status. Personal details restricted. | CSWDO and receiving offices               |\n| REC-F06   | Recovery monitoring matrix                          | Fields in Annex 5-D.                                                                                    | Recovery monitoring unit                  |\n| REC-F07   | Build-back-better screening checklist               | Cause of damage, siting, design, inclusion, environment findings, decision, conditions, verification.   | Proponent office; reviewers               |\n| REC-F08   | Recovery feedback and grievance log                 | Channel, category, barangay, routing, reply, status. Personal details restricted.                       | Feedback desk                             |\n| REC-F09   | Recovery closeout and outcome evaluation record     | PPA closeout evidence, outcome findings, lessons, Chapter 7 corrective actions.                         | Recovery monitoring unit                  |\n| Annex 5-A | IAT and Master Requirements traceability register   | Indicator rows, scores, priority, MR links, owners, targets, status.                                    | CDRRMO MOO custodian                      |\n| Annex 5-B | Recovery RACI with legal decision authority         | RACI with a separate legal-authority column.                                                            | CDRRMO; City Legal Office                 |\n| Annex 5-C | Pre-disaster recovery framework outline             | Contents of the framework document.                                                                     | CDRRMO; CPDO                              |\n| Annex 5-D | Recovery monitoring matrix fields                   | Minimum fields of REC-F06.                                                                              | Recovery monitoring unit                  |\n| Annex 5-E | Minimum data for the recovery baseline              | Data, disaggregation and source.                                                                        | CDRRMO Research and Planning              |\n\n# 19. Relationship with Other Chapters\n\n**Table 5.37**\n\n*Interfaces With the Other Chapters of the Manual*\n\n| **Ch.** | **Subject**                                                               | **Chapter 5 interface**                                                                                                        |\n|---------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Legal Mandate, DRRM Governance and Institutional Accountability           | CDRRMC and Mayor decision rights; State of Calamity procedure; full disclosure.                                                |\n| 2       | CDRRMO Organizational Structure, Staffing and Human Resource Management   | Research and Planning function and the planned PDNA positions; staff welfare after events.                                     |\n| 3       | Risk Intelligence, Planning and Institutional Preparedness                | CDRA, scenarios and contingency plans; recovery annex attached to each plan; PSCP and LDRRMP.                                  |\n| 4       | Early Warning, EOC Activation, Incident Management and Emergency Response | RDANA and SitReps; SOP 4-09 deactivation; ER-F05 transition register and ER-F06 AAR, received by SOP 5-03.                     |\n| 6       | DRRM Financing, Resource Management and Accountability                    | All fund sources, budget review, procurement, donations, insurance and audit for recovery PPAs.                                |\n| 7       | Monitoring, Evaluation, Knowledge Management and Continuous Improvement   | Outcome evaluation, AAR integration, corrective-action register and knowledge products.                                        |\n| 8       | Stakeholder Engagement and Institutional Partnerships                     | MOAs with private sector, CSOs, academe and development partners; RDRRMC VIII and national agencies; Part C interface offices. |\n| 9       | Public Awareness, Community Resilience and Capacity Development           | PDNA and recovery planning training; community participation; recovery IEC.                                                    |\n| 10      | Institutional Sustainability, Deep Resilience and Recognition             | Recovery performance as evidence for long-term resilience and recognition (for example, Gawad KALASAG).                        |\n\n# 20. Conclusion\n\nChapter 5 continues the operational chain of Chapter 4 past the closing of the EOC. It makes recovery a planned system: the City prepares before the event, receives the response handover item by item, assesses damage and needs through a written decision route, prepares and approves a program that builds back better, delivers services through the offices that hold the mandates, and tracks every project to completion. Its central control is traceability: each recovery action can be traced from the PDNA need to the approved PPA, the BBB screen, the fund source, the output on the ground and the lesson learned.\n\nWriting these procedures does not implement them. Institutionalisation requires an adopted pre-disaster recovery framework, a designated and trained PDNA team, a decision on the recovery committee, a signed referral agreement, a working monitoring matrix and at least one exercise or real event in which the procedures were used and reviewed. Until then, this chapter remains a controlled working draft.\n\n# References\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2023). *Ormoc City disaster risk reduction and management ten-year plan (2023–2032)*.\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2026a). *Ormoc CDRRMO–EOC institutional assessment tool* (Version 1.7) \\[Unpublished assessment workbook\\]. Repository source: reference/Ormoc_CDRRMO-EOC_Institutional_Assessment_Tool_v1-7.xlsx.\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2026b). *Ormoc CDRRMO–EOC master requirements traceability and 140-indicator data dictionary* (Version 1.2) \\[Unpublished project reference workbook\\].\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2026c). *Ormoc City CDRRMO–EOC manual of operations, Chapter 4: Early warning, EOC activation, incident management and emergency response* (Draft 1.2).\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2026d). *MODE platform coherence analysis, Pareto priority indicators, and final 10-chapter MOO/EOC manual structure* \\[Unpublished project document\\].\n\nDepartment of Social Welfare and Development, Department of the Interior and Local Government, Department of Health, & Department of Education. (2021). *Joint Memorandum Circular No. 2, s. 2021: Guidelines on camp coordination and camp management and internally displaced persons protection*.\n\nHousing and Land Use Regulatory Board & Climate Change Commission. (n.d.). *Supplemental guidelines on mainstreaming climate change and disaster risks in the comprehensive land use plan*.\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2020). *National disaster risk reduction and management plan 2020–2030*.\n\nNational Economic and Development Authority. (2020). *Disaster rehabilitation and recovery planning guide*. ISBN 978-971-8535-27-1.\n\nOffice of Civil Defense. (n.d.). *Post-disaster needs assessment guidance notes* \\[Current edition to be obtained from OCD Region VIII\\].\n\nPresidential Decree No. 1096. (1977). *National Building Code of the Philippines*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 656. (1951). *Property Insurance Law*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 7160. (1991). *Local Government Code of 1991*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 7279. (1992). *Urban Development and Housing Act of 1992*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 10121. (2010). *Philippine Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Act of 2010*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 10173. (2012). *Data Privacy Act of 2012*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 11036. (2018). *Mental Health Act*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 12009. (2024). *New Government Procurement Act*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 12076. (2024). *Ligtas Pinoy Centers Act*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 12145. (2025). *Economy, Planning and Development Act*.\n\nUnited Nations Office for Disaster Risk Reduction. (2015). *Sendai framework for disaster risk reduction 2015–2030*.\n\nUnited Nations Office for Disaster Risk Reduction. (2017). *Disaster resilience scorecard for cities: Detailed level assessment*.\n\n# Validation and Source Control Register\n\n**Table 5.38**\n\n*Validation and Source Control Register*\n\n| **Validation item**                                | **Required action before approval**                                                                                                                                                                    | **Responsible institution / reviewer**         |\n|----------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------|\n| **IAT v1.7 A9, A8.7, A10.6, A3.4 and Part C rows** | Rows copied into Annex 5-A (12 November 2026). Validate scores and evidence at the December 2026 workshop; all rows are "Pending validation".                                                          | CDRRMO / assessment team                       |\n| **Workbook chapter labels**                        | The "Feeds Manual Chapter" column reads "MOO Ch.8" for A9 rows; update the crosswalk in generate_seed.py so A9 rows map to Chapter 5 under the adopted structure.                                      | Platform data custodian                        |\n| **Chapter 4 cross-references**                     | Done: Chapter 4 Draft 1.2 (12 November 2026) refers to recovery as Chapter 5 and to financing as Chapter 6.                                                                                            | CDRRMO MOO custodian                           |\n| **SOP and annex numbering**                        | The drafted financing chapter (MOO_Ch5v1_v1.0) uses SOPs 5-01 to 5-10 and Annexes 5-A to 5-C. Renumber them to 6-xx when it becomes Chapter 6, before this chapter is seeded, so codes do not collide. | CDRRMO MOO custodian / platform data custodian |\n| **Approval route for the program**                 | Confirm CDRRMC and Sanggunian roles, interim approval of priority PPAs and the route to the NDRRMC.                                                                                                    | City Legal Office; OCD VIII; DEPDev VIII       |\n| **Recovery committee**                             | Decide whether to create a Rehabilitation and Recovery Committee or assign the function to the CDRRMP TWG (EO 2022-00020); confirm lead offices.                                                       | CDRRMC; City Legal Office                      |\n| **PDNA and RDANA issuances**                       | Obtain the current OCD PDNA Guidance Notes and RDANA issuance (the guide cites NDRRMC MC No. 25, 2014).                                                                                                | OCD VIII / CDRRMO                              |\n| **NDRRMF access rules**                            | Confirm the current NDRRMF rules (period covered, LDRRMF-insufficiency condition, proposal route).                                                                                                     | OCD VIII; DBM                                  |\n| **DSWD issuances**                                 | Confirm current issuances on cash-for-work and emergency shelter assistance.                                                                                                                           | CSWDO                                          |\n| **Yolanda damage figure**                          | The 10-Year Plan prints PHP 8,000,000,000,000.00; obtain the correct figure from the DRRM Plan 2016–2020.                                                                                              | CDRRMO Research and Planning                   |\n| **Housing office name**                            | Confirm the office named "OCHO" in the 10-Year Plan and its mandate for the shelter sub-committee.                                                                                                     | HRMO / Mayor''s Office                          |\n| **Barangay denominator**                           | Use the PSGC barangay list (85 as of 31 July 2025) pending the CPDO, City Secretary and DILG CLGOO reconciliation.                                                                                     | CPDO / City Secretary / DILG CLGOO             |\n| **Privacy**                                        | DPO review of REC-F05 and REC-F08, consent wording and retention periods.                                                                                                                              | City DPO                                       |\n| **COA trust-fund citation**                        | Verify the COA Circular 2012-002 section on trust-fund transfers before citing it in recovery financing (carried from Chapter 6).                                                                      | City Accountant; COA auditor                   |\n'
